/-!
# Odd-field symplectic and orthogonal FF quotients

The faithful-image reduction retains the actual full linear normalizer,
its offender, and the concrete simple central quotient. The offender acts
faithfully by conjugation on the image, without an inner-offender assumption.
The rank-one symplectic carrier is identified with PSL₂; the odd parameters
5, 7 and 9 have actual alternating or characteristic-two quotient models.

The general odd-field theorem remains open. Higher-rank cross-characteristic
FF exclusions and the surviving small orthogonal and symplectic carrier
comparisons must still be proved. In particular, PSp₄(3) cannot be removed
by its family label, and the orthogonal rank-one and minus rank-two entries
remain part of the required catalogue. The full rank-one symplectic case
reduces to PSL₂ recognition with the exact linear parameter predicate.
Covering-group lifting is separate from this quotient problem.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, B.1.11–13, printed pp.72–74 in
`refs/quasithin.pdf`, citing Guralnick–Malle, *Classification of 2F-modules,
II*, Table 2, DOI 10.1515/9783110198126.117. No classification theorem from
that table is assumed in these reductions.
-/
